hadiths[85]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27451","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from Ayyub from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Asma, she said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings into my house. He said: Spend, and do not tie up, lest it be tied up against you."
"27452","Sufyan from Hisham from his father from his mother, she said: My mother came to me, desirous, in the treaty of Quraysh, while she was a polytheist, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes."
"27453","Yunus said: Layth - meaning Ibn Sad - narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Asma, the like of it, and he said: While she was a polytheist, in the treaty of Quraysh and their truce when they made treaty with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27454","Hasan said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us that he heard Urwah narrating from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came while she was a polytheist in the treaty of Quraysh when they made treaty with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother has come while she is desirous; shall I maintain ties with her? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"27455","Abdullah ibn Idris said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his father, that Asma bint Abi Bakr said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, until when we were at al-Arj, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted, and Aishah sat beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I sat beside my father. And the provisions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the provisions of Abu Bakr were one, with the slave boy of Abu Bakr. So Abu Bakr sat waiting for him to appear to him, and he appeared without his camel with him. So he said: Where is your camel? He said: I lost it last night. So Abu Bakr said: One camel, you lose it? And he began beating him, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Look at this pilgrim and what he does."
"27456","Muhammad ibn Fudayl said: Yazid - meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad - narrated to us from Mujahid, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said: Perform Hajj alone and leave the saying of this one - meaning Ibn Abbas. So Ibn al-Abbas said: Will you not ask your mother about this? So he sent to her, and she said: Ibn Abbas spoke the truth; we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, and he ordered us, so we made it Umrah, and everything lawful became lawful for us, until the censers blazed between women and men."
"27457","Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a daughter who is a bride, and she was struck by measles, so her hair fell out; shall I join hair to it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined."
"27458","Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a horse and ate from it."
"27459","Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman is struck by menstrual blood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her scrape it, then let her rub it with water, then let her pray in it."
"27460","Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife; is there sin upon me if I falsely claim from my husband what he did not give me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who falsely claims what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"27461","Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Spend - or: give - or: disburse, and do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you; and do not count, lest Allah count against you."
"27462","Aththam ibn Ali Abu Ali al-Amiri said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah from Asma, she said: We were indeed commanded with freeing slaves in the eclipse prayer."
"27463","Muawiyah ibn Amr said: Zaidah narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma, she said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed ordered us with freeing slaves in the prayer of the solar eclipse."
"27464","Ibn Numayr said: Hisham narrated to us from Fatimah from Asma, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I entered upon Aishah and said: What is the matter with the people praying? So she pointed with her head to the sky. So I said: A sign? She said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prolonged the standing very much, until faintness covered me, so I took a waterskin beside me and began pouring water on my head. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, and the sun had cleared, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows: There is nothing I had not seen except I have seen it in this station of mine, even Paradise and Hell. It has been revealed to me that you will be tried in the graves, close to - or: like - the trial of the False Messiah; I do not know which of the two Asma said. One of you is brought, and it is said: What is your knowledge of this man? As for the believer - or: the certain; I do not know which of the two Asma said - so he says: He is Muhammad, he is the Messenger of Allah; he came to us with clear proofs and guidance, so we answered and followed - three times. So it is said to him: We knew you believed in him, so sleep righteous. And as for the hypocrite - or: the doubter; he does not know which of the two Asma said - so he says: I do not know; I heard the people saying something, so I said it."
"27465","Ibn Numayr from Hisham from Fatimah from Asma, she said: When a woman with fever was brought to her for her to supplicate for her, she poured water between her and her bosom, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to cool it with water, and he said: It is from the heat of Hell."
"27466","Abu Usamah from Hisham from Fatimah from Asma, she said: We broke our fast in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cloudy day in Ramadan, then the sun appeared. I said to Hisham: Were they ordered to make it up? He said: There is no escape from that."
"27467","Abu Usamah said: Hisham narrated to us from his father and Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma, she said: I made the travel provisions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Abu Bakr when he intended to emigrate. She said: We did not find anything to tie his provisions and his waterskin with. She said: So I said to Abu Bakr: By Allah, I find nothing to tie it with except my waistband. He said: So he said: Split it in two, and tie the waterskin with one and the provisions with the other. So for that she was named Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
"27468","Yahya ibn Said from Hisham, he said: Fatimah narrated to me from Asma, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife; is there sin upon me if I falsely claim from my husband other than what he gives me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who falsely claims what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"27469","Yahya ibn Said from Hisham, he said: Fatimah narrated to me from Asma, she said: We ate the meat of a horse of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27470","Yahya ibn Said from Hisham, he said: Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrated to me, and Waki said: Hisham narrated to us from Fatimah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman from the Ansar said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have a little daughter who is a bride, and her hair fell out; is there sin upon me if I join her head? He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined."
"27471","Yahya ibn Said from Hisham, he said: Fatimah narrated to me from Asma, and Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham narrated to us from Fatimah from Asma, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: One of us has menstrual blood strike her garment. She said: She scrapes it, then let her rub it with water, then let her sprinkle it, then pray in it."
"27472","Waki said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate its meat - or: from its meat."
"27473","Ibn Numayr from Hisham from Fatimah from Asma, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Spend - or: give - and do not count, lest Allah count against you; and do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"27474","Muhammad ibn Bishr said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr - and she was one who counted - and from Abbad ibn Hamzah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Spend - or: disburse - or: give generously, like this and like this, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you; and do not count, lest Allah count against you."
"27475","Attab ibn Ziyad said: Abdullah - meaning Ibn al-Mubarak - narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We used to give Zakat al-Fitr in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), two mudds of wheat, with the mudd you eat with."
"27476","Abu Usamah said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father informed me from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: Al-Zubayr married me, and he had on earth no wealth, nor slave, nor anything except his horse. She said: So I used to feed his horse, and suffice him its care, and manage it, and crush date stones for his camel, and knead, and draw water, and stitch his bucket, and knead dough, and I did not know how to bake, so neighbor women from the Ansar used to bake for me, and they were truthful women. And I used to carry date stones from the land of al-Zubayr which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had granted him, on my head, and it was two-thirds of a farsakh from me. She said: So I came one day with the date stones on my head, and I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of his Companions, so he called me, then said: Ikh, ikh, to carry me behind him. She said: So I was shy to go with the men, and I remembered al-Zubayr and his jealousy. She said: And he was the most jealous of people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew I was shy, so he went on. And I came to al-Zubayr and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me with date stones on my head, and with him a group of his Companions, and he made his camel kneel for me to ride with him, but I was shy, and I knew your jealousy. So he said: By Allah, your carrying the date stones is harder upon me than your riding with him. She said: Until Abu Bakr sent to me after that a servant girl, and she sufficed me the care of the horse, so it was as if he had freed me."
"27477","Abu Usamah from Hisham from his father from Asma, that she carried Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr at Makkah. She said: So I went out while I was full-term, and I came to Madinah and alighted at Quba, and I gave birth to him at Quba, then I came with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed him in his lap, then he called for a date and chewed it, then spat in his mouth, so the first thing that entered his belly was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Then he rubbed his palate with a date, then supplicated for him and blessed him, and he was the first child born in Islam."
"27478","Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim said: Abu Aqil - meaning Abdullah ibn Aqil al-Thaqafi - narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father informed me from his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me in the truce of Quraysh as a polytheist, while she was desirous - meaning needy - so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me while she is a polytheist, desirous; shall I maintain ties with her? He said: Maintain ties with your mother."
"27479","Ibn Numayr said: Hisham narrated to us from his father from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me while she was a polytheist, in the treaty of Quraysh when they made treaty, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come while she is desirous; shall I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"27480","Yahya ibn Said from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, informed me from Asma, that she alighted at the house of Muzdalifah, and said: O my son, has the moon set on the night of Jam while she was praying? I said: No. So she prayed a while, then said: O my son, has the moon set? He said: And the moon had set. I said: Yes. She said: So depart. So we departed, then we went with her until we stoned the Jamrah, then she returned and prayed Fajr in her dwelling. So I said to her: O dear, we have prayed in the dark. She said: No, O my son, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the weak women."
"27481","Yahya ibn Said from Abd al-Malik, he said: Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, narrated to us from Asma, he said: She brought out to me a Tayalisi cloak with a band of Kisrawani brocade a span wide, and its openings edged with it. She said: This is the cloak of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he used to wear it. It was with Aishah, and when Aishah passed away, I took it to me. So we wash it for our sick to seek healing by it."
"27482","Yunus ibn Muhammad said: Aban - meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar - narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Nothing is more jealous than Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"27483","Yazid ibn Harun from Hajjaj from Abu Umar, the freedman of Asma, he said: Asma brought out to us a cloak buttoned with brocade, and said: In this the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to meet the enemy."
"27484","Hushaym said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a Tayalisi cloak whose band was Kisrawani brocade."
"27485","Rawh said: Shubah narrated to us from Muslim al-Qurri, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the temporary enjoyment of Hajj, and he permitted it, and Ibn al-Zubayr used to forbid it. So he said: This is the mother of Ibn al-Zubayr narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it, so enter upon her and ask her. He said: So we entered upon her, and she was a large blind woman, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed permitted it."
"27486","Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muslim, brother of al-Zuhri, informed me from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr from Asma, she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you who believes in Allah and the Last Day raise her head until we raise our heads, lest they see the private parts of the men because of the shortness of their waist-wrappers. And they at that time used to wrap with this striped garment."
"27487","Ibrahim ibn Khalid said: Rabah narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from some of them from a freedman of Asma from Asma, that she said: The Muslims were needy; they used to wrap with this striped garment, and it only reached half their shanks or about that. So I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day - meaning the women - let her not raise her head until we raise our heads, lest she look at the private parts of the men because of the shortness of their waist-wrappers."
"27488","Abd al-Ala from Mamar from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, brother of al-Zuhri, from a freedman of Asma from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day - then he mentioned the hadith."
"27489","Affan said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Rashid narrated to me from the nephew of al-Zuhri from a freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr from Asma, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of women, whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until the men raise their heads. She said: And that was because their waist-wrappers were short, lest their private parts be uncovered when they prostrated."
"27490","Surayj ibn al-Numan said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of women, whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not raise her head until the Imam raises his head, because of the tightness of the garments of the men."
"27491","Ubaydah ibn Humayd from Yazid ibn Ziyad from Mujahid from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered us, so we made it Umrah, and we became fully lawful, until the censers blazed between women and men."
"27492","Ibn Numayr said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his grandmother - I do not know whether Asma bint Abi Bakr or Suda bint Awf - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib and said: What prevents you from Hajj, O aunt? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a sick woman, and I fear being held back. He said: Then enter ihram and stipulate that your release is where you are held back."
"27493","Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I was told from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alarmed on the day the sun eclipsed, so he took a coat of mail until he reached his cloak, and he stood with the people a long standing, standing then bowing. She said: So I began looking at the woman who was older than me standing, and at the woman who was sicker than me standing, and I said: I am more deserving to endure the long standing than you."
"27494","And Ibn Jurayj said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alarmed."
"27495","Yahya ibn Ishaq said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reciting, while he was praying toward the Corner, before he proclaimed what he was commanded: So which of the favors of your Lord would you deny."
"27496","Yaqub said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me from his father from his grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at Dhi Tuwa, Abu Quhafah said to a young daughter of his: O my little daughter, take me up to Abu Qubays. She said: And his sight had gone. She said: So I took him up upon it. So he said: O my little daughter, what do you see? She said: I see a crowd gathered. He said: Those are the cavalry. She said: And I see a man running among that crowd, coming and going. He said: O my little daughter, that is the warder - meaning who orders the cavalry and goes before them. Then she said: By Allah, the crowd has spread. So he said: By Allah, when the cavalry has charged, hurry with me to my house. So she went down with him, and the cavalry met him before he reached his house, and on the neck of the girl was a collar of hers of silver, so the man met him and snatched it from her neck. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah and entered the mosque, Abu Bakr came to him with his father visiting him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said: Would you not have left the old man in his house until I come to him in it? Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, he is more deserving to walk to you than for you to walk to him. He said: So he seated him before him, then wiped his chest, then said to him: Submit. So he submitted. And Abu Bakr brought him in, may Allah be pleased with him, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his head was like thaghamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change this from his hair. Then Abu Bakr stood and took the hand of his sister and said: I adjure by Allah and by Islam the collar of my sister. So no one answered him. So he said: O my little sister, count your collar as lost."
"27497","Yaqub said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that his father narrated to him from his grandmother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and Abu Bakr went out with him, Abu Bakr carried all his wealth with him, five thousand dirhams or six thousand dirhams. She said: And he went with it with him. She said: So our grandfather Abu Quhafah came to us, and his sight had gone, and said: By Allah, I see he has stricken you with his wealth along with himself. She said: I said: No, O father, he has left for us much good. She said: So I took stones and left them, and placed them in the niche of the house where my father used to place his wealth, then placed a garment over them, then took his hand and said: O father, place your hand on this wealth. She said: So he placed his hand upon it and said: No harm; if he has left this for you, he has done well, and in this is sufficiency for you. She said: No, by Allah, he left us nothing, but I wanted to quiet the old man by that."
"27498","Hasan said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when she made tharid, she covered it a little until its heat went, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is greater for blessing."
"27499","Qutaybah ibn Said said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us from Uqayl, and Attab said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwah from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when she made tharid, she covered it, then he mentioned the like of it."
"27500","Yunus said: Imran ibn Yazid al-Qattan, a Basran, narrated to us from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman from his mother from Asma, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married my daughter, then she fell ill and her head shed, and her husband has come to me; shall I join her head? She said: So he cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined."
"27501","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Yazid narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from his mother, from Asma, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entering ihram for Hajj, and she said: He said to us: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him remain in his ihram, and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram."
"27502","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, he said: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Muhajir say: I heard Ibn Abbas say to Ibn al-Zubayr: Will you not ask your mother? He said: So we entered upon his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr, and she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until when we were at Dhu al-Hulayfah, he said: Whoever among you wishes to enter ihram for Hajj, let him enter ihram, and whoever among you wishes to enter ihram for Umrah, let him enter ihram. Asma said: I, Aishah, al-Miqdad, and al-Zubayr were among those who entered ihram for Umrah."
"27503","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Nafi, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed during the eclipse. She said: He prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then stood and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then lifted and prolonged the standing, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then lifted, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then stood and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then lifted and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then lifted, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then lifted, then prostrated and prolonged the prostration, then finished, and said: Paradise drew near to me, such that had I dared I would have brought you a bunch from its bunches, and Hell drew near to me, such that I said: O Lord, and I am among them, and there was a woman - Nafi said: I think he said: a cat was clawing her - I said: What is the matter with her? It was said to me: She confined it until it died; she neither fed it nor let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth."
"27504","Waki narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he stood and prayed; he prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then lifted and prolonged the standing, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then lifted and prolonged the standing, then prostrated two prostrations, then did in the second the like of that, then said: Paradise was brought near to me, such that had I dared upon it I would have brought you a bunch from its bunches, and Hell was brought near to me, such that I said: O Lord, and I am among them, and I saw in it a cat - he said: I think she was clawing a woman - who had confined it and did not feed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth until it died."
"27505","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, and she is his mother, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We went out in ihram, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him complete, and Rawh said: let him remain in his ihram, and whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram. She said: I did not have a sacrificial animal with me, so I exited ihram, and al-Zubayr, her husband, had a sacrificial animal with him, so he did not exit ihram. She said: I put on my clothes and exited ihram, and came to al-Zubayr, and he said: Keep away from me. She said: I said: Are you afraid I will pounce on you?"
"27506","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, the freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr, informed us, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she said: O my son, has the moon set on the night of Muzdalifah? I said: No. Then she said: O my son, has the moon set? I said: Yes. She said: Then depart. So we departed, then went on until she stoned the Jamrah, then returned and prayed Fajr in her dwelling. I said to her: We have departed very early. Rawh said: meaning O dear one. She said: No, O my son, the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave permission to the weak women."
"27507","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, that al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr after her son Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr was killed, and said: Your son apostatized in this House, and Allah, Exalted and Glorious, made him taste a painful punishment and did with him what He did. She said: You lie; he was dutiful to his parents, fasting, praying at night. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed us that there will emerge from Thaqif two liars, the latter of the two worse than the former, and he is the destroyer."
"27508","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was alarmed on the day the sun eclipsed, so he took a coat of armor until he was reached with his cloak, and stood with the people a long standing, standing then bowing; had a man come after the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had bowed, he would not have known he had bowed, he would not have imagined he had bowed, due to the length of the standing. She said: I kept looking at the woman older than me and the woman sicker than me standing, and I am more entitled to endure the length of standing than them."
"27509","Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad and Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, both from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me that Urwah informed him that Asma informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the pulpit say: There is nothing more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Glorious. And Yunus said in his hadith from Aban: Nothing is more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Glorious."
"27510","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me, he said: I heard Asma bint Abi Bakr say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was counting something and measuring it. He said: O Asma, do not count, lest Allah count against you. She said: I did not count anything after the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether it left me or came to me, and whatever of Allah's provision ran out with me, Allah, Exalted and Glorious, replaced it."
"27511","Hashim narrated to us, he said: My father Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say while on the pulpit: There is nothing more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Glorious."
"27512","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that Asma said: I used to serve al-Zubayr, her husband, and he had a horse; I used to tend it, and nothing of service was harder on me than tending the horse. I used to gather fodder for it, attend to it, tend it, and crush date-stones for it. He said: Then she obtained a servant whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave her. She said: She sufficed me the tending of the horse and relieved me of its burden."
"27513","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say while on the pulpit: Nothing is more jealous than Allah, Exalted and Glorious."
"27514","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book this hadith in his handwriting: Said, meaning Ibn Sulayman Sadawayh, narrated to us, he said: Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarah, from his father, he said: When al-Hajjaj killed Ibn al-Zubayr and crucified him upside down, while he was on the pulpit, Asma came with a slave girl leading her, having lost her sight, and said: Where is your commander? He mentioned a story, then she said: You lie, but I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will emerge from Thaqif two liars, the latter of the two more evil than the former, and he is the destroyer."
"27515","Yaamar narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Abdullah, the freedman of Asma, narrate that he heard Asma bint Abi Bakr say: I have with al-Zubayr two armlets of brocade which the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him to fight in."
"27516","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn al-Munkadir, he said: Asma used to narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: He said: When a man enters his grave, if he was a believer, his deeds surround him - prayer and fasting. He said: The angel comes to him from the direction of prayer and it repels him, and from the direction of fasting and it repels him. He said: He calls to him: Sit. He said: He sits, and says to him: What do you say about this man, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Who? He said: Muhammad. He said: I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He says: How do you know? Did you perceive him? I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah. He said: He says: Upon that you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be resurrected. He said: And if he was wicked or a disbeliever, he said: The angel comes and there is nothing between him and him to repel him. He said: He seats him, he says: Sit, what do you say about this man? He said: Which man? He said: Muhammad. He said: He says: By Allah, I do not know; I heard the people say something and I said it. He said: The angel says to him: Upon that you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be resurrected. He said: A beast is set upon him in his grave, with it a whip whose lash is a coal like the hump of a camel; it strikes him as Allah wills, deaf, not hearing his voice to have mercy on him."
"27517","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Fatimah narrated to me, from Asma, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a co-wife, so is there any sin upon me if I falsely claim satisfaction from my husband beyond what he gives me? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who falsely claims what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood."
"27518","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Asma, she said: We ate a horse of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"27519","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman of the Ansar said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I have a young daughter, a bride, and her hair has fallen out in tufts; is there any sin upon me if I join her head with extensions? And Waki said: her hair fell out. He said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who asks for it."
"27520","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings to me; shall I give from it? He said: Give, and do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"27521","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Fatimah narrated to me, and Abu Muawiyah said: Hisham narrated to me, from Fatimah, from Asma, that a woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: One of us has her garment stained with menstrual blood. He said: She scrapes it, then rubs it with water, then sprinkles it, then prays in it."
"27522","Waki narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abu Umar, the freedman of Asma, he said: Asma said: O slave girl, hand me the cloak of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: She brought out a cloak of Tayalisah."
"27523","Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ate its meat, or from its meat."
"27524","Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman and Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ward, two men of the people of Makkah, narrated to us, who heard it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Al-Zubayr is a strict man, and the poor come to me and I give them charity from his house without his permission. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give, and do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"27525","Waki narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"27526","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hajjaj, from Abu Umar, the freedman of Asma, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a cloak of Tayalisah edged with brocade in which he met the enemy."
"27527","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr narrated to me, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings into my house; shall I give from it? He said: Give, and do not tie up, lest Allah tie up against you."
"27528","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr informed him, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, the like of it."
"27529","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, from the freedman of Asma, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a cloak of Tayalisah whose facing was Khusrawani brocade."
"27530","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Spend, or scatter, and do not count, lest Allah count against you, or do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you."
"27531","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, and she was one who counted, and from Abbad ibn Hamzah, from Asma, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Spend, or pour forth, or scatter, like this and like this, and do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you, and do not count, lest Allah count against you."
"27532","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard the clamor of the people saying: a sign, and we that day were in alarm. I went out wrapped in a cloak of al-Zubayr's until I entered upon Aishah, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was standing praying for the people. I said to Aishah: What is the matter with the people? She motioned with her hand to the sky. She said: I prayed with them, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had finished his first prostration. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood a long standing, until I saw some of those praying sprinkling themselves with water, then bowed a long bowing, then stood and did not prostrate, a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then bowed a long bowing, shorter than his first bowing, then prostrated, then gave salam while the sun had cleared. Then he ascended the pulpit and said: O people, the sun and moon are two signs of Allah's signs; they do not eclipse for anyone's death nor life. When you see that, hasten to prayer, to charity, and to remembrance of Allah. O people, nothing remains that I had not seen except I have seen it in this station of mine, and you have been shown to me being tried in your graves: one of you is asked: What did you say, and what did you worship? If he says: I do not know; I saw the people say something and I said it, and do something and I did it, it is said to him: Yes, upon doubt you lived and upon it you died; this is your seat in Hell. And if he says: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, it is said: Upon certainty you lived - he said: you died - this is your seat in Paradise. And I have seen fifty or seventy thousand entering Paradise in the form of the moon on the night of full moon. A man stood to him and said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make him among them. O people, you will not ask me about anything until I descend except I will inform you of it. A man stood and said: Who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so, to whom he used to be attributed."
"27533","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Umar, a son-in-law of Ata, that Asma brought out for us a cloak buttoned with brocade; she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he met war, used to wear this."
"27534","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: My mother came to me, desirous, while she was a polytheist, during the treaty of Quraysh and their truce between them and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me, desirous, while she is a polytheist; shall I maintain ties with her? He said: Maintain ties with her. He said: And I think she was her foster mother."
"27535","Attab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: We used to give Zakat al-Fitr in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two mudds of wheat by the mudd you measure your food with."
